# name: Cadence drills
# description: Spin-ups at easy power: one minute each at 95, 105 and 115 rpm, then a fast minute at 120+, four times. Smooth pedaling, no bouncing.
duration,power,power_end,cadence,text
10:00,45,70,,Warm up
1:00,60,,95,95 rpm (set 1/4)
1:00,60,,105,105 rpm
1:00,62,,115,115 rpm
1:00,65,,120,120+ rpm
3:00,55,,85,Normal cadence
1:00,60,,95,95 rpm (set 2/4)
1:00,60,,105,105 rpm
1:00,62,,115,115 rpm
1:00,65,,120,120+ rpm
3:00,55,,85,Normal cadence
1:00,60,,95,95 rpm (set 3/4)
1:00,60,,105,105 rpm
1:00,62,,115,115 rpm
1:00,65,,120,120+ rpm
3:00,55,,85,Normal cadence
1:00,60,,95,95 rpm (set 4/4)
1:00,60,,105,105 rpm
1:00,62,,115,115 rpm
1:00,65,,120,120+ rpm
3:00,55,,85,Normal cadence
10:00,60,40,,Cool down
# name: Endurance 90 min
# description: Zone 2 by power: 70 minutes at 68 % of FTP, the base of every training plan. Steady, conversational.
duration,power,power_end,cadence,text
10:00,45,70,,Warm up
70:00,68,,90,Endurance
10:00,60,40,,Cool down
# name: FTP test 20 min
# description: Warm up with a 5-minute effort, then 20 minutes all out with the trainer free (a flat road: shift as you like). Your FTP is about 95 % of the 20 minutes' average power.
# ftp_test: 95% of 20:00 after 31:00
